.TH REDSTONE 1 "2026" "redstone 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redstone \- a SQLite shell with zsh-style completion, drop-in for sqlite3(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redstone
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ database ]
.RI [ sql\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B redstone
is an interactive and batch SQL shell for SQLite, built to be run wherever
.BR sqlite3 (1)
is run today.
Every dot command, output mode and command-line flag that
.BR sqlite3 (1)
accepts is either implemented to the same behaviour or refused with an
explicit message, never silently ignored (see
.B PARITY
below); an
.B alias sqlite3=redstone
is meant to survive a normal day's work.
.PP
On top of that baseline,
.B redstone
adds a zsh-style completion menu (table, column and dot-command names,
narrowed as you type and browsed with the arrow keys or Tab), live
syntax highlighting of the statement being typed, a colour theme system,
and output that is easier to read by default \(em box-drawn tables with
headers and colour, sized to the terminal, rather than
.BR sqlite3 (1)'s
plain
.B |\-separated
batch format. The
.B \-\-compat
flag turns all of that off and reproduces
.BR sqlite3 (1)'s
behaviour exactly.
.PP
With no
.I database
argument, an in-memory database is used, exactly as in
.BR sqlite3 (1).
Any
.I sql
arguments after the database name are executed as a batch, after which
.B redstone
exits; with none, it opens the interactive prompt (or reads statements
from standard input, if that is not a terminal).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the redstone and linked SQLite version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-compat
Format results exactly as
.BR sqlite3 (1)'s
batch mode does: \fBlist\fR output mode, \fB|\fR column separator, headers
off, no colour, no box drawing. Also turns off screen-width auto-detection
(see
.B \-screenwidth
below). Everything downstream of this flag is covered by a byte-exact
differential test suite against the real
.BR sqlite3 (1)
binary.
.TP
.BI \- MODE
Start in \fIMODE\fR: one of
.BR ascii ", " box ", " column ", " csv ", " html ", " json ", " line ", "
.BR list ", " markdown ", " quote ", " table ", " tabs .
(\fB.mode\fR inside the shell accepts a larger set, including \fBinsert\fR,
\fBtcl\fR and \fBqbox\fR, that
.BR sqlite3 (1)
itself does not accept as a command-line flag either.)
.TP
.BI \-init " FILE"
Read \fIFILE\fR instead of the default init files
(\fB~/.sqliterc\fR and the redstone-specific \fBredstonerc\fR, see
.B FILES
below).
.TP
.B \-noinit
Read no init file and no theme file: "no configuration" means all of it,
not just the SQLite half.
.TP
.BI \-cmd " COMMAND"
Run \fICOMMAND\fR (a dot command or a SQL statement) after the init files
and before reading standard input. May be given more than once; they run
in the order given.
.TP
.BR \-batch ", " \-interactive
Force batch or interactive mode regardless of whether standard input is a
terminal.
.TP
.BR \-echo ", " \-header ", " \-noheader ", " \-bail ", " \-stats
Echo each statement before running it; force column headers on or off;
stop on the first error; print row-count/timing statistics after each
statement.
.TP
.B \-readonly
Open the database read-only.
.TP
.B \-safe
Refuse commands capable of doing damage outside the database file itself
(\fB.shell\fR, \fB.system\fR, writing outside the working directory, and
similar) \(em intended for running an untrusted script.
.TP
.BI \-nonce " STRING"
Pairs with \fB.nonce\fR: a command prefixed with the matching nonce is
exempt from \fB\-safe\fR for that one line.
.TP
.BI \-separator " SEP"
.TQ
.BI \-nullvalue " TEXT"
.TQ
.BI \-newline " SEP"
Set the column separator, the text printed for a NULL value, and the row
separator, the same as the like-named \fB.\fR commands.
.TP
.BI \-screenwidth " N" ", " \-sw " N"
Fix the terminal width used to shrink wide columnar output to \fIN\fR
(minimum 2), the same as \fB.mode \-\-screenwidth N\fR. Without this flag,
interactive non-\fB\-\-compat\fR mode auto-detects the real terminal width
via the controlling tty and re-reads it before every result, so resizing
the window takes effect on the next query; \fB\-\-compat\fR and this flag
both turn auto-detection off, which is what keeps \fB\-\-compat\fR output
byte-identical to a fixed-width run of
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.SH OUTPUT MODES
Set with \fB\-MODE\fR on the command line or \fB.mode MODE\fR inside the
shell. The default, interactive or not, is \fBbox\fR with headers and
colour; \fB\-\-compat\fR switches the default to \fBlist\fR with headers
off, matching
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.PP
Byte-for-byte parity with the linked
.BR sqlite3 (1)
binary under \fB\-\-compat\fR is asserted by the test suite (\fBmake
parity\fR) for the thirteen classic modes: \fBascii box column csv html
insert json line list markdown quote table tabs\fR. The remaining modes
.RB ( c ", " count ", " jatom ", " jobject ", " off ", " psql ", " qbox ", "
.BR split ", " tcl )
are best-effort.
.PP
Each mode accepts option flags after its name, e.g.
.BR ".mode box --wrap 40 --screenwidth 100" ;
see \fB.help mode\fR inside the shell for the full set.
.SH DOT COMMANDS
Commands beginning with \fB.\fR configure the session rather than querying
the database, exactly as in
.BR sqlite3 (1).
Run
.B .help
inside the shell for the complete, current list with one-line
descriptions \(em duplicating it here would only let this page drift out
of sync with the binary. Commands used most often:
.TP
.BI \.mode " MODE"
Set the output mode (see \fBOUTPUT MODES\fR).
.TP
.BI \.tables\ ? PATTERN ?
List tables.
.TP
.BI \.schema\ ? PATTERN ?
Show \fBCREATE\fR statements.
.TP
.BI \.import " FILE TABLE"
Import CSV or delimited data.
.TP
.BI \.dump\ ? PATTERN ?
Render the database as SQL.
.TP
.BI \.open " FILE"
Close the current database, open another.
.TP
.B \.headers \fRon|off
Toggle column headers.
.TP
.BI \.width " N N ..."
Set fixed per-column widths.
.PP
Two commands are redstone-specific, not part of
.BR sqlite3 (1):
.TP
.B .theme \fR[\fINAME\fR|\fIFILE\fR]
With no argument, print the active palette as a loadable theme file. With
a name (\fBdark\fR, \fBlight\fR, \fBbasic\fR, \fBno\-color\fR) or a file
path, load that theme for the session.
.TP
.B .editor \fRemacs|vi
Switch the line-editor's keymap without restarting.
.PP
Eleven commands that would need an upstream SQLite extension this build
does not vendor
.RB ( .archive ", " .recover ", " .expert ", " and similar)
are recognised and refused with a message naming what they need, rather
than being silently accepted and doing nothing.
.SH PARITY
.B redstone \-\-compat
is meant to be indistinguishable from
.BR sqlite3 (1)
for scripting: same flags, same dot commands, same byte output. Where it
knowingly is not \(em an extension SQLite build this binary lacks, a mode
the shipped
.BR sqlite3 (1)
binary itself rejects, and similar \(em the difference is refused loudly
rather than silently approximated. Outside \fB\-\-compat\fR, redstone is
intentionally not upstream: prettier output, a completion menu, and
highlighting are the reason to run it instead.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.sqliterc
Read at startup unless \fB\-init\fR, \fB\-noinit\fR or \fB\-cmd\fR redirect
it; for parity with
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/redstone/redstonerc \fR(or \fB~/.config/redstone/redstonerc\fR)
Read after \fB~/.sqliterc\fR, so a setting here wins over the same setting
there. redstone-specific: not read by
.BR sqlite3 (1).
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/redstone/theme \fR(or \fB~/.config/redstone/theme\fR)
The colour theme file, in the format \fB.theme\fR with no argument
prints. Also suppressed by \fB\-noinit\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Any non-empty value disables colour output, overriding theme detection.
.TP
.B TERM
.B dumb
disables colour and Unicode box drawing (ASCII borders are used
instead); a non-tty output stream disables colour regardless of
.BR TERM .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for \fBredstonerc\fR and the theme file; see
.B FILES
above.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on a clean exit or a script's last statement succeeding;
.B 1
on a SQL error with \fB\-bail\fR or in the default non-interactive
"stop on error" behaviour that matches
.BR sqlite3 (1);
.B 2
on a command-line usage error (unknown or malformed option).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B redstone mydb.db
Open \fBmydb.db\fR interactively with completion, highlighting and box
output.
.TP
.B redstone --compat mydb.db "SELECT * FROM t;" > out.txt
Run one query in a script exactly as
.BR sqlite3 (1)
would.
.TP
.B redstone -box -screenwidth 100 mydb.db
Force box output shrunk to fit a 100-column terminal regardless of the
real one, e.g. when piping into a fixed-width report.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1)
.SH BUGS
Parity is asserted automatically only for the thirteen classic output
modes and the dot commands this build implements; a difference in a
best-effort mode is a documentation gap, not silently accepted behaviour
\(em see the project's own gap list in \fBPROJECT.md\fR for the current,
complete set.
